{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 50,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD, Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the bill of your mother's divorcement, whom I have put away? or which of my creditors ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to whom I have sold you? Behold, for your iniquities have ye sold yourselves, and for your transgressions is your mother put away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why, when I came, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no man? when I called, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none to answer? Is my hand shortened at all, that it cannot redeem? or have I no power to deliver? behold, at my rebuke I dry up the sea, I make the rivers a wilderness: their fish becometh putrid, because ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no water, and dieth for thirst.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I clothe the heavens with blackness, and I make sackcloth their covering.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Lord GOD hath given me the tongue of the learned, that I should know how to speak a word in season to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " weary: he wakeneth morning by morning, he wakeneth my ear to hear as the learned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD GOD opened my ear, and I was not rebellious, neither turned away back.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I gave my back to the smiters, and my cheeks to them that plucked off the hair: I hid not my face from shame and spitting.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the Lord GOD will help me; therefore shall I not be confounded: therefore have I set my face like a flint, and I know that I shall not be ashamed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " near that justifieth me; who will contend with me? let us stand together; who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my adversary? let him come near to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold the Lord GOD will help me; who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall condemn me? lo, they all shall wax old as a garment; the moth shall eat them up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among you that feareth the LORD, that obeyeth the voice of his servant, that walketh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " darkness, and hath no light? let him trust in the name of the LORD, and rely upon his God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.50.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.50.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, all ye that kindle a fire, that encompass ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yourselves",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with sparks: walk in the light of your fire, and in the sparks ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye have kindled. This shall ye have of my hand; ye shall lie down in sorrow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
